WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:17.952
The Week Five outline explicitly includes a LUCAS practical. This lesson uses all seven saved sections of the matching AET supplement, including its glossary and readiness material. The supplement entry itself has topic-matched, not explicit-directory, placement.
第5周周纲明确包括LUCAS实操。本课使用相应AET补充课保存的全部七节，包含术语及备用状态内容；该补充入口本身是按主题对应，并非目录明确分配。

00:00:17.952 --> 00:00:30.960
The aim is to select and integrate mechanical support without losing useful CPR, correct positioning or patient assessment. Simply getting the machine onto a manikin is not the whole school objective.
目标是筛选并整合机械支持，同时不丢掉有效CPR、正确位置和患者评估。仅仅把机器装到模型上，并不是全部学习目标。

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:45.192
Official LUCAS Three version three point one instructions were checked for the relevant procedures and figures. Actual school version, setup options and hands-on checkoff still require the instructor and training unit.
已核对LUCAS 3版本3.1官方说明中的相关步骤和图示。实际学校版本、设置选项及动手考核，仍须由教师和训练器械确认。

00:00:45.192 --> 00:00:59.568
School wording, manufacturer instructions and service permission are kept distinct. A device lesson does not automatically authorize a PCP to deploy a device that the current service procedure headings allocate to advanced crews.
学校措辞、厂家说明和机构权限会分别标明。器械教学不会自动授权PCP，去部署现行机构流程标题分配给高级团队的器械。

00:00:59.568 --> 00:01:11.976
Manual compression quality can deteriorate with fatigue, awkward positioning or movement. A suitable device can reduce some of those logistical problems and free attention for other essential tasks.
手动按压质量可能因疲劳、别扭位置或移动而下降。合适器械可减轻其中部分操作困难，让人员有余力处理其他关键任务。

00:01:11.976 --> 00:01:25.536
However, a machine can be misplaced, can fail and can consume valuable treatment time during application. It is not accurate to describe its compressions as flawless or its circulation as guaranteed.
但机器可能位置不对、发生故障，也可能在安装时消耗宝贵治疗时间。不能把其按压描述为无瑕，也不能保证其产生的循环。

00:01:25.536 --> 00:01:40.368
Current AHA adult guidance does not recommend routine mechanical CPR for every arrest. It allows consideration in selected settings where effective manual compressions are difficult or dangerous, with strict interruption control.
现行AHA成人指导不建议每次骤停都常规机械CPR，但允许在有效手动按压困难或危险的特定环境中考虑，并严格控制停顿。

00:01:40.368 --> 00:01:53.232
Therefore explain the specific problem this deployment solves. Device availability alone is not the indication, and mechanical support is not a reason to abandon manual CPR competence or renewal.
所以应说清这次部署要解决什么具体问题。现场有器械本身不是指征，机械支持也不是放弃手动CPR能力或更新训练的理由。

00:01:53.232 --> 00:02:05.760
Coronary perfusion pressure describes the driving pressure for myocardial blood flow. During CPR it is commonly considered as the difference between aortic and right atrial pressure during relaxation.
冠状动脉灌注压描述驱动心肌血流的压力。在CPR中，通常考虑舒张或放松阶段主动脉压与右心房压之差。

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:17.640
That explains why recoil, adequate depth and short interruptions matter. It does not mean that a routine noninvasive cuff or ETCO2 display directly measures this gradient.
这能解释回弹、适当深度和短停顿为何重要，但不意味着普通无创血压袖带或ETCO2显示直接测量这一压差。

00:02:17.640 --> 00:02:30.936
The school uses numerical examples for pressure and rebuilding after a pause. Treat them as physiology illustrations, not a universally measured minimum that proves this individual will achieve ROSC.
学校用压力数字及停顿后的重建来举例，应理解为生理说明，而不是一个在此患者身上实测、能证明一定ROSC的统一最低值。

00:02:30.936 --> 00:02:44.808
The practical consequence is to minimize avoidable no-flow and observe actual performance. A piston moving at a regular rate cannot by itself establish that the myocardium or brain is receiving sufficient blood.
实操意义是减少可避免的无血流，并观察真实表现。活塞有规律地运动，本身无法证明心肌或脑已得到足够血液。

00:02:44.808 --> 00:02:59.976
The saved school material teaches broad device knowledge. Current public PR31 has an ACP-and-above applicability heading and selected nontraumatic medical-arrest situations. Those facts must remain visible together.
保存的学校材料教授较广器械知识；现行公开PR31适用标题为ACP及以上，并限定部分非创伤内科骤停情境。这两项事实必须同时保留。

00:02:59.976 --> 00:03:12.624
Manufacturer personnel recommendations also require CPR competence and specific LUCAS training. Reading this slide is neither the complete instructions nor a practical performance evaluation.
厂家人员建议也要求CPR能力及LUCAS专门训练。读过本页，既不等于读完说明书，也不等于接受实际表现评估。

00:03:12.624 --> 00:03:24.624
A school instructor can supervise the required laboratory demonstration while explaining the later service boundary. Do not relabel a supervised learner exercise as independent field permission.
学校教师可以监督要求的实验示范，并解释之后的机构边界。不能把监督下学员练习重新说成独立现场许可。

00:03:24.624 --> 00:03:39.768
If an existing device accompanies a patient, confirm the actual trained personnel, transport plan and local requirements. The existence of the device does not automatically make any receiving crew competent or authorized to operate it.
患者已有器械时，要确认真正受训人员、转运计划及当地要求。机器已经在身上，不会自动让任何接手团队都具备操作能力和权限。

00:03:39.768 --> 00:03:53.328
The manufacturer intended population is an adult in circulatory arrest where external compressions are expected to help. Confirm the clinical indication and the more specific service selection before applying the frame.
厂家目标人群是外部按压可能有益的成人循环骤停。安装框架前，要确认临床指征及更具体的机构筛选。

00:03:53.328 --> 00:04:09.984
For a too-small fit, the specified three quick signals and inability to enter the required operating state mean manual CPR must resume. The school seventeen-centimeter reference concerns chest fit, not the patient standing height or sternum length.
尺寸太小时，规定的三次快速提示及无法进入所需工作状态，意味着应恢复手动CPR。学校提到的十七厘米与胸部适配有关，不是患者身高或胸骨长度。

00:04:09.984 --> 00:04:23.136
For a too-large fit, do not press the frame down onto the chest merely to engage the locks. Body weight alone is not the manufacturer fit test; correct safe placement and closure are what matter.
尺寸太大时，不能为了扣锁把框架压进胸部。单凭体重并不是厂家的适配测试，关键是能否安全正确定位与扣合。

00:04:23.136 --> 00:04:40.392
The supplement calls chest trauma a caution, but local PR31 excludes traumatic arrest. Pregnancy, unusual anatomy, recent surgery or a difficult position also require the appropriate specific pathway and safe fit, not improvised universal permission.
补充课把胸部创伤列为注意事项，但当地PR31排除创伤性骤停。妊娠、特殊解剖、近期手术或困难体位，也需要适用专门流程及安全适配，不能临时编成通用许可。

00:04:40.392 --> 00:04:54.600
Identify the back plate, upper unit, support legs, claw locks and release rings on the actual training device. Knowing the name is useful only if you can identify what must connect and what must stay unobstructed.
应在实际训练器械上辨认背板、上部机体、支腿、爪锁和释放环。只有能指出什么要连接、什么不能受阻，名称才有实际用处。

00:04:54.600 --> 00:05:07.536
The suction cup contains the pressure pad and is a disposable component in the reviewed instructions. Its outer edge and the pressure pad are related but not identical anatomical references.
已核对说明中，吸盘内有按压垫，并属于一次性组件。吸盘外缘和按压垫有关，但不是同一个解剖参考点。

00:05:07.536 --> 00:05:20.568
The stabilization system helps maintain alignment between patient and device. It is not a rigid spinal immobilizer, and the frame does not become an approved torso-protection cage after ROSC.
稳定系统帮助保持患者与器械对齐，不是刚性脊柱固定器；ROSC后，框架也不会因此变成获准的躯干保护笼。

00:05:20.568 --> 00:05:32.400
The patient wrist straps and stabilization straps are not lifting slings. Prepare the actual transport support and team technique rather than attempting to carry a patient by these straps.
患者腕带和稳定带不是吊运带。应准备真实转运支撑及团队技术，不能试图靠这些带子把患者提起来。

00:05:32.400 --> 00:05:46.248
ADJUST allows the compression interface to be positioned. PAUSE after adjustment establishes the start state, while PAUSE during compressions stops the mechanism at that state. ACTIVE starts the chosen compression mode.
ADJUST用于调整按压接触部分；调整后按PAUSE建立起始状态，按压中按PAUSE则在该状态停止机构。ACTIVE启动所选按压模式。

00:05:46.248 --> 00:06:01.152
Those are functional distinctions, not a guarantee of one identical physical movement on every unit. Version three point one allows setup options that affect automatic adjustment, rates, ventilation alerts and pauses.
这些是功能区别，不保证每台器械都有完全相同的物理动作。版本3.1可有影响自动调整、频率、通气提示及暂停的配置选项。

00:06:01.152 --> 00:06:15.024
Keep hands and other body parts away from moving compression components. A displayed mode must be checked together with the actual mechanism and patient position, not trusted as the sole sign of effective CPR.
手及其他身体部位应离开运动的按压组件。显示模式必须结合实际机构运动和患者位置核查，不能只凭模式判断CPR有效。

00:06:15.024 --> 00:06:29.904
The original diagram separates normal state changes from the manual fallback. In particular, a planned battery replacement from PAUSE returns to PAUSE under the preserved-state conditions, not to ADJUST as one school sentence claims.
原创图把正常状态转换与手动备用方案分开。尤其要注意，在保留状态条件内，从PAUSE开始的计划换电后回到PAUSE，而非学校某句所写的ADJUST。

00:06:29.904 --> 00:06:44.424
Before deployment, confirm an appropriate charged battery, a ready spare, correct accessories and an undamaged device. The required battery remains installed even when an approved external power source is connected.
部署前，应确认合适且已充电的电池、备用电池、正确附件及无损器械。即使接了获准外部电源，所需电池仍须装在机内。

00:06:44.424 --> 00:06:57.720
Verify the cup and straps, unobstructed ventilation openings and the availability of the back plate. A charged motor without the plate or required disposable is not a ready resuscitation system.
核对吸盘、带子、通风口畅通及背板可用。电机有电但缺背板或所需一次性组件，不能算复苏系统已就绪。

00:06:57.720 --> 00:07:11.568
Power-up includes a self-test and a ready indication. Know the actual training device response before the event. A failed self-test is not a prompt to repeatedly experiment while the patient receives no compressions.
开机包含自检及就绪提示。事件前就要知道实际训练器械如何响应。自检失败并不是让患者无按压地等着自己反复试验的提示。

00:07:11.568 --> 00:07:24.480
Preparation also means assigned people and manual backup. The safest device team is the one that can quickly continue effective manual CPR when the machine is unavailable or unsuitable.
准备也包括人员分工和手动备用方案。最安全的器械团队，是机器不可用或不合适时，能迅速继续有效手动CPR的团队。

00:07:24.480 --> 00:07:37.968
Recognize arrest and start manual CPR immediately; do not wait for the LUCAS case to open. Effective manual care and prompt indicated defibrillation remain active while the device is prepared.
识别骤停后立即开始手动CPR，不要等LUCAS箱打开。准备器械期间，应继续有效手动照护及快速有指征除颤。

00:07:37.968 --> 00:07:51.096
Plan who supports the head, places the back plate, attaches the frame, confirms the cup and restarts effective compressions. Make readiness and commands audible before any required pause.
先计划谁支持头部、谁放背板、谁扣框架、谁确认吸盘、谁恢复有效按压，并在必要停顿前清楚通报准备状态及口令。

00:07:51.096 --> 00:08:04.752
The school summary asks for no more than ten seconds of interruption, while an earlier passage tolerates under twenty. We retain the tighter stated training target and do not teach twenty seconds as a harmless allowance.
学校总结要求停顿不超过十秒，但前段又容许二十秒以内。这里保留较严格的已述训练目标，不把二十秒教成无害额度。

00:08:04.752 --> 00:08:16.584
Practice accurate placement and safe checks together with speed. A seven-second median from trained teams is not a guarantee for a novice or permission to skip the fit and lock check.
应同时练准确定位、安全核查和速度。受训团队七秒中位数，不是新手保证，也不是省略适配及锁定检查的许可。

00:08:16.584 --> 00:08:29.544
The reviewed instructions describe a small coordinated upper-body lift or side-to-side roll to place the back plate immediately below the armpits. Support the head and use the actual trained team technique.
已核对说明描述通过协调的小幅上半身抬起或左右翻滚，把背板放在腋下紧邻处。应支持头部，并使用实际受训团队技术。

00:08:29.544 --> 00:08:40.464
Positioning the plate accurately now makes central cup placement easier later. A low or off-center plate should not be accepted merely because the frame can be clicked onto it.
背板此时准确，之后吸盘更容易居中。不能只因框架扣得上，就接受过低或偏侧背板。

00:08:40.464 --> 00:08:50.112
Resume manual compressions as soon as the plate is placed. Do not hold the patient without CPR while another rescuer searches the case for the upper unit.
背板放好后尽快恢复手动按压，不能在另一人翻箱寻找上部机体时，让患者一直没有CPR。

00:08:50.112 --> 00:09:04.536
For unusual anatomy, injury or movement risk, the instructor must demonstrate the appropriate method on the training setup. This explanation is not a universal lifting authorization for any patient or environment.
特殊解剖、损伤或移动风险时，应由教师在训练设置中示范适当方法。本讲解不是对任何患者及环境都通用的搬运许可。

00:09:04.536 --> 00:09:16.536
Open the claw locks using the release rings, then let go so the locks can engage. Clothing or sheets must not obstruct the connection. Keep fingers away from the locking mechanism.
用释放环打开爪锁后要松手，让锁能够扣合。衣物和床单不能挡住连接，手指应离开锁定机构。

00:09:16.536 --> 00:09:30.360
The manufacturer describes coordinated near-side attachment while manual compressions continue, followed by the brief interruption needed to attach the other side. Learn this with the actual frame and partner positions.
厂家描述先在手动按压继续时协调扣近侧，再短暂停顿完成另一侧。应使用真实框架及搭档位置学习。

00:09:30.360 --> 00:09:41.976
Listen for engagement and check the joined parts as instructed, rather than accepting one click as proof that both sides are secure. Never force closure by precompressing the chest.
应按说明听到扣合并检查连接，不能听到一次响就认为两侧全牢固，也不能为扣合而预压胸部。

00:09:41.976 --> 00:09:54.384
If the frame cannot be safely attached, return immediately to manual CPR. Troubleshooting a latch must not create an extended pause in the only treatment currently moving blood.
框架无法安全安装时，应立即恢复手动CPR。不能为了排查锁扣，长时间中断当下唯一在推动血流的治疗。

00:09:54.384 --> 00:10:06.960
The pressure pad must act at the appropriate sternal compression point. The reviewed manufacturer figure uses the lower outer edge of the cup immediately above the end of the sternum as a positioning reference.
按压垫必须作用于适当胸骨按压点。已核对厂家图用吸盘下方外缘紧邻胸骨末端上方，作为定位参考。

00:10:06.960 --> 00:10:19.584
Do not confuse that outer rim with the center of the pressure pad or use the nipple as a universal landmark. Patient anatomy and the actual device must be identified, not guessed from clothing.
不能把外缘与按压垫中心混为一谈，也不能把乳头当通用标志。必须识别患者解剖和真实器械，不能隔着衣服猜。

00:10:19.584 --> 00:10:29.784
Incorrect position can worsen injury and impair circulation. A rapid transition with the compression point too low is not a successful practical performance.
位置错误可能增加损伤并妨碍循环。如果按压点过低，即使转换很快，也不算实操成功。

00:10:29.784 --> 00:10:42.648
Show the instructor both the landmark and your reason for it, then verify after the start and after every meaningful movement. Correct initial placement is not proof that the device will remain correct.
应向教师指出标志并解释理由，启动后及每次重要移动后再核对。最初位置正确，并不能证明之后一直正确。

00:10:42.648 --> 00:10:54.792
In the reviewed default workflow, adjust the cup until the pressure pad contacts the chest without pressing it down. Then use PAUSE to establish the start position before activating the selected mode.
在已核对的默认流程中，调整吸盘，使按压垫接触胸部而不把胸压下，再用PAUSE建立起始位置，之后启动所选模式。

00:10:54.792 --> 00:11:06.192
Version three point one has optional automatic fitting and height behavior. QuickFit is not a promise that an incorrectly centered device or an unsafe patient fit will correct itself.
版本3.1可选自动适配及高度行为。QuickFit并不保证位置偏了或患者尺寸不安全时，机器会自行纠正。

00:11:06.192 --> 00:11:19.080
Check the actual state and location before starting, keep hands clear and observe the initial compressions. If the cup shifts or the start position is wrong, use the correct adjustment sequence promptly.
启动前核对真实状态和位置，手离开活动区域，并观察最初按压。吸盘移位或起始位置不对时，应迅速按正确调整顺序处理。

00:11:19.080 --> 00:11:31.680
If safe correct positioning cannot be achieved, restore manual CPR instead of repeatedly pressing ACTIVE. A device refusing a state can be a safety signal, not a control to defeat.
不能取得安全正确位置时，应恢复手动CPR，不能反复按ACTIVE。器械拒绝进入某状态可能是安全提示，不是要强行克服的控制。

00:11:31.680 --> 00:11:46.056
Apply the stabilization strap once the device is operating correctly, avoiding a new unnecessary compression pause. The reviewed arrangement places a cushion behind the neck near the shoulders and connects it to the support straps.
器械正确工作后再安装稳定带，避免新增不必要按压停顿。已核对结构把垫子放在颈后靠肩处，并接到支腿带上。

00:11:46.056 --> 00:11:56.736
This is not an instruction to wrap or tighten a restraint around the airway. Demonstrate the actual cushion, buckle path and appropriate securing on the training device.
这并不是把束带绕气道收紧的指令。应在训练器械上示范真实垫子、扣合路径和适当固定。

00:11:56.736 --> 00:12:08.712
Prevent twisting, hold the device appropriately during securing and verify that the cup remains at the intended point. A strap can stabilize a wrong position just as effectively as a right one.
固定时避免扭转并适当稳住器械，再确认吸盘仍位于目标点。带子可能把错误位置固定得和正确位置一样牢。

00:12:08.712 --> 00:12:21.840
The manufacturer explicitly allows delaying strap application if it prevents or delays needed medical treatment. Keep the priority on effective resuscitation rather than completing every accessory first.
厂家明确允许在安装稳定带会妨碍或延迟必要治疗时暂缓。优先是有效复苏，而不是先把所有附件都装完。

00:12:21.840 --> 00:12:35.616
The default thirty-to-two mode pauses after thirty compressions to allow two breaths. The airway operator must anticipate the pause and deliver appropriate breaths rather than beginning preparation only when the machine stops.
默认30:2模式在三十次按压后暂停供两次送气。气道操作者应提前准备并给适当通气，不能机器停了才开始准备。

00:12:35.616 --> 00:12:48.648
Continuous mode supports ongoing compressions with asynchronous ventilation under the appropriate advanced-airway pathway. The reviewed default alert is ten times per minute, but actual settings can differ.
连续模式在适当高级气道流程下支持持续按压和异步通气。已核对默认提示为每分钟十次，但实际配置可能不同。

00:12:48.648 --> 00:13:04.152
A tube or SGA label does not prove effective ventilation. Reassess seal, chest rise, airway position and waveform; a significant leak or failed breath requires a coordinated change, not simply faster bagging.
气管或SGA名称不能证明有效通气。应复评密合、胸廓起伏、气道位置和波形；明显漏气或送气失败，需要协调改变，而不是单纯更快挤球。

00:13:04.152 --> 00:13:16.104
If the airway plan changes, communicate and select the appropriate compression mode with the team. The timing light does not assess chest rise and cannot protect the patient from excessive volume.
气道计划改变时，应通报并与团队选择适当按压模式。时序灯不会评估胸廓起伏，也无法防止过大送气量。

00:13:16.104 --> 00:13:27.840
Mechanical compressions create ECG artifact. The reviewed LUCAS instructions require a brief PAUSE before ECG analysis, with the interruption kept as short as possible.
机械按压会产生ECG伪差。已核对LUCAS说明要求分析ECG前短暂PAUSE，并尽量缩短停顿。

00:13:27.840 --> 00:13:43.368
The manufacturer permits defibrillation during device operation when the defibrillator instructions and local protocol allow it. That does not mean the rhythm can be reliably analyzed during compressions, or that people may keep touching the patient during discharge.
厂家允许在除颤器说明及当地流程允许时，于器械运行中除颤。但这不代表按压中能可靠分析心律，也不代表放电时人员可以继续接触患者。

00:13:43.368 --> 00:13:57.576
The school drill pauses, analyzes, clears, shocks if indicated and immediately restarts. Preserve the locally instructed sequence and distinguish its steps from the broader manufacturer capability statement.
学校练习采用暂停、分析、确认离开、有指征时电击，再立即恢复。应保留当地所教顺序，并与厂家较广功能描述区分。

00:13:57.576 --> 00:14:10.848
Keep pads and wires outside the compression contact area, check position after a shock and explicitly confirm that compressions have resumed. Do not leave the machine paused while everybody watches the ECG.
电极及线缆应避开按压接触区，电击后检查位置，并明确确认按压已恢复。不能所有人都看ECG，而机器一直停着。

00:14:10.848 --> 00:14:26.328
Mechanical support can operate during selected movement if patient and device are safely supported and the correct position and angle remain maintained. This is a condition, not a blanket instruction to carry every arrest immediately.
患者与器械有安全支撑，并能保持正确位置和角度时，机械支持可在部分移动中运行。这是条件，不是让每个骤停都立即搬走的通用指令。

00:14:26.328 --> 00:14:41.472
The school passage suggests a pause for critical transfers; the manufacturer allows ongoing compressions when its conditions are met. Plan the actual move and any necessary interruption rather than adding a routine pause without a reason.
学校段落建议关键转移时暂停；厂家则在条件满足时允许运行。应规划真实移动及必要停顿，而不是无理由常规再加一次暂停。

00:14:41.472 --> 00:14:55.968
Use the trained lifting and transport method, not wrist straps or stabilization straps as handles. Protect airway tubing, vascular access, the head and the team, and observe for shifting or blocked ventilation openings.
应使用受训搬运与转运方法，不能把腕带或稳定带当提手。保护气道管、血管通路、头部和团队，并观察移位及通风口受阻。

00:14:55.968 --> 00:15:07.944
If safe alignment cannot be maintained, act immediately to restore effective appropriate CPR. Patient movement is not evidence that the device maintained good compressions throughout the move.
无法保持安全对齐时，应立即恢复有效且适当的CPR。患者已经搬动，并不能证明移动全程器械都保持了好按压。

00:15:07.944 --> 00:15:19.896
The reviewed manufacturer gives a typical initial battery runtime of about forty-five minutes for a nominal patient. Do not assume every battery in service will provide exactly that duration.
已核对厂家给出名义患者情况下初始电池续航通常约四十五分钟。不能以为服役中的每块电池都精确达到这一时长。

00:15:19.896 --> 00:15:31.728
Watch the actual battery and alarm indications. Distinguish an intermittent low-charge warning from the end-of-service-life indication and from a high-priority stopped-device alarm.
应观察实际电池和报警指示，并区分间歇低电量、寿命结束提示，以及导致器械停止的高优先级报警。

00:15:31.728 --> 00:15:43.776
The device requires its approved battery even with external power. Use only the specified compatible source and protect cables; an improvised power connection is not a safe backup.
即使外接电源，器械也需要获准电池。应使用规定相容电源并保护线缆，临时改装电源不是安全备用方案。

00:15:43.776 --> 00:16:00.360
The school gives a single two-hour recharge estimate, but the reviewed IFU distinguishes charging in the device from the external charger, with different maximum times. Read the actual charging instructions and verify charge instead of relying on elapsed time.
学校给单一两小时充电估计，但已核对说明区分机内和外部充电器，并列不同最长时间。应读实际充电说明并确认电量，不能只看过了多久。

00:16:00.360 --> 00:16:12.696
Prepare the charged replacement before the swap. In the reviewed planned sequence, press PAUSE, remove the old battery, insert the charged battery and wait for the green PAUSE indication.
换电前先准备已充电替换电池。已核对的计划流程是按PAUSE、取出旧电池、装入新电池，并等绿色PAUSE指示。

00:16:12.696 --> 00:16:26.808
The school sentence claiming the unit returns to ADJUST at its previous height is incorrect for this preserved-state sequence. The manufacturer table returns PAUSE to PAUSE when the battery is replaced within the specified memory interval.
学校说换电后回到原高度ADJUST的句子，不适用于这项保留状态流程。厂家表格规定，在所述记忆时限内更换，从PAUSE回到PAUSE。

00:16:26.808 --> 00:16:43.800
That memory interval is less than sixty seconds; it is not an acceptable sixty-second CPR pause. If it is exceeded, a self-test and resetting the start position are required. Maintain a manual fallback rather than watching the clock with no compressions.
记忆时限是少于六十秒，不是允许CPR停六十秒。超过后需要自检并重设起始位置。应保持手动备用方案，不能无按压地只看钟。

00:16:43.800 --> 00:16:58.224
Verify the actual state and cup position, then restart the appropriate ACTIVE mode promptly. A routine planned swap differs from stopping a malfunctioning device, where removal and immediate manual CPR take priority.
确认真实状态和吸盘位置后，迅速重启适当ACTIVE模式。常规计划换电，与故障时停止器械不同；故障应优先移除并立即手动CPR。

00:16:58.224 --> 00:17:11.424
A high-priority malfunction can stop compressions. The reviewed warning directs stopping the device, removing it and starting manual compressions immediately if operation is abnormal or compressions are insufficient.
高优先级故障可能使按压停止。已核对警告要求，运行异常或按压不足时应停止、移除器械，并立即开始手动按压。

00:17:11.424 --> 00:17:25.080
Do not allow a prolonged no-flow interval while several rescuers troubleshoot. Assign a focused equipment task while effective manual care continues, and use qualified service support for a persistent fault.
不能让多人排故时产生长时间无血流。有效手动照护继续时，再分配具体器械任务；持续故障应交合格维修支持。

00:17:25.080 --> 00:17:38.184
A mute control silences a signal for a period; it does not fix the fault, recharge a battery or restart circulation. Distinguish an audible warning from proof of actual compression performance.
静音控制只会暂时消掉声音，不会修好故障、给电池充电或恢复循环。应区分报警声音与实际按压表现证据。

00:17:38.184 --> 00:17:53.760
Repositioning a shifted cup and responding to a failed motor are different problems. If safe, prompt correction cannot restore a reliable state, use manual CPR rather than repeatedly trying to make the machine appear normal.
纠正吸盘移位，与处理电机故障，是不同问题。如果迅速安全纠正仍不能恢复可靠状态，应使用手动CPR，不能反复尝试只让机器看起来正常。

00:17:53.760 --> 00:18:08.664
When spontaneous circulation is appropriately confirmed, stop unnecessary mechanical compressions and announce the post-arrest transition. An organized rhythm or a compression-generated pulse alone is not that confirmation.
适当确认自主循环后，应停止不必要机械按压，并宣布进入骤停后照护。单有规则心律或按压造成的脉搏，不构成这种确认。

00:18:08.664 --> 00:18:21.984
The school calls leaving the locked device on every post-ROSC patient a gold standard. The reviewed IFU does not establish that universal claim, so it is not taught as a mandatory rule here.
学校把所有ROSC患者都保留锁定器械称为金标准，但已核对说明并未确立这一通用主张，所以这里不把它教成强制规则。

00:18:21.984 --> 00:18:37.392
If the device remains temporarily for the authorized plan, ensure it does not impair ventilation, chest expansion or comfort, and keep checking the patient and actual state. Follow the relevant team decision for adjustment or removal.
如果按获授权计划暂时保留，必须确认不妨碍通气、胸廓扩张或舒适，并持续核查患者与真实状态。调整或移除应依相应团队决定。

00:18:37.392 --> 00:18:49.872
A prior height setting must be reverified after patient or device movement before any later restart. Being one button away does not remove the need to confirm re-arrest, fit and position.
患者或器械移动后，之后再次启动前必须重新核实原高度。所谓只差一个按钮，并不会取消确认再次骤停、适配和位置的要求。

00:18:49.872 --> 00:19:03.456
Effective CPR can sometimes support enough cerebral blood flow for movement or apparent awareness without sustained spontaneous circulation. The school glossary names this CPR-induced consciousness.
有效CPR有时可支持足够脑血流，使患者活动或看似有意识，却没有持续自主循环。学校术语把它称为CPR诱发意识。

00:19:03.456 --> 00:19:15.144
Treat a new movement as an important patient change requiring appropriate assessment, not automatic proof that the arrest has ended. Distinguish it from a mechanical twitch during shock delivery.
新活动是需要适当评估的重要患者变化，不是骤停已经结束的自动证明，也应与电击时机械性抽动区分。

00:19:15.144 --> 00:19:30.864
Current N02 places consideration of sedation for CPR-induced consciousness in the ACP interventions. It is not an independent PCP drug instruction, and paralysis alone would not provide comfort or unconsciousness.
现行N02把CPR诱发意识时考虑镇静列在ACP干预中。这不是PCP独立用药指令，单纯肌松也不会提供舒适或失去意识。

00:19:30.864 --> 00:19:42.936
Coordinate effective care, protect the patient and team and obtain the appropriate support. Do not simply switch off all circulation support or silence distress to make the device workflow easier.
应协调有效照护、保护患者和团队，并请求适当支持。不能只为让器械流程容易，就关闭全部循环支持或把痛苦表现压下去。

00:19:42.936 --> 00:19:55.656
Removal may follow a planned transition, unsafe fit or malfunction. State which situation applies because the urgent manual fallback and a controlled post-event removal have different priorities.
移除可能发生在计划转换、适配不安全或故障后。应说明属于哪一种，因为紧急手动备用与事件后有控制移除的优先事项不同。

00:19:55.656 --> 00:20:09.792
The reviewed removal sequence powers off, disconnects the stabilization neck section and releases the upper part from the plate using the release rings. Use the actual unit and avoid trapping lines or body parts.
已核对移除顺序为关机、断开稳定系统颈垫部分，再用释放环把上部机体与背板分开。应使用实际器械，并防止夹住管路或身体。

00:20:09.792 --> 00:20:20.232
Remove the back plate only if the patient condition allows it. Do not disrupt airway, perfusion support or a safe transport plan simply to complete equipment cleanup.
只有患者情况允许时才取背板，不能只为完成器械收拾而打断气道、灌注支持或安全转运计划。

00:20:20.232 --> 00:20:32.208
When CPR is still indicated and the machine cannot safely provide it, manual compressions resume immediately. Equipment handling must be coordinated around that clinical priority.
仍有CPR指征而机器无法安全提供时，应立即恢复手动按压，器械处理必须围绕这一临床优先事项协调。

00:20:32.208 --> 00:20:45.984
The reviewed LUCAS Three instructions and school supplement direct replacing the used disposable suction cup. Older PR31 wording discusses cleaning and reuse, so that conflict must not be hidden.
已核对LUCAS 3说明及学校补充课要求更换已用一次性吸盘，而较旧PR31文字讨论清洁和重复使用，因此不能隐藏这一冲突。

00:20:45.984 --> 00:21:02.568
Use the actual approved device and infection-control instructions. For reusable surfaces and straps, use the compatible process and disinfectant handling directions; do not infer a mixing recipe or contact time from an ambiguous bleach label.
应使用实际获准器械及感染控制说明。可重复用表面和带子，要按相容处理及消毒剂说明；不能凭含糊的漂白剂标签推断配比或接触时间。

00:21:02.568 --> 00:21:14.616
Do not immerse the device or allow liquid into the housing. Inspect for damage, let appropriate components dry, replace required disposables and recharge or replace the battery.
不能浸泡器械或让液体进入机壳。应检查损伤，让相应组件干燥，更换所需一次性物品，并充电或换电池。

00:21:14.616 --> 00:21:28.464
A cleaned appearance is not the entire readiness check. Verify completeness, correct cup attachment, straps, open locks, power and the self-test according to the routine and post-use checks.
看起来干净并不是全部备用检查，还要按常规和使用后检查确认组件齐全、吸盘安装、带子、锁扣打开、电源及自检。

00:21:28.464 --> 00:21:42.120
Document when manual and mechanical compressions began or stopped, why the device was selected, the operating modes and significant interruptions. Do not count a silent stopped machine as ongoing CPR.
记录手动及机械按压开始或停止时间、选择器械理由、运行模式及重要停顿，不能把安静停下来的机器算作持续CPR。

00:21:42.120 --> 00:21:56.256
Include fit or position problems, movement checks, battery changes, alarms, fallback and the patient response. A device record helps but cannot establish every clinical finding or human action automatically.
应包括适配或位置问题、移动核查、换电、报警、备用方案及患者反应。器械记录有帮助，但不能自动证明全部临床发现或人的行动。

00:21:56.256 --> 00:22:11.616
The reviewed device can send status/use data when powered off, depending on configuration. Transmission can also receive settings, so use the authorized process; this course does not upload patient data or change a real device.
已核对设备可依配置在关机状态发送状态及使用数据。传输也可能接收设置，因此要用获授权流程；本课程不会上传患者数据或更改真实器械。

00:22:11.616 --> 00:22:26.160
For a fault, follow reporting, quarantine and qualified service procedures rather than returning an unreliable unit to the case. Record readiness honestly so the next crew does not inherit a hidden problem.
故障应按报告、停用隔离及合格维修流程处理，不能把不可靠设备放回箱就结束。要真实记录备用状态，避免下一团队接手隐藏问题。

00:22:26.160 --> 00:22:42.096
In this original supervised station, start effective manual CPR on a suitable adult manikin. Prepare and apply the device using named roles, anatomical checks and measured interruptions, not just a total assembly time.
本原创监督下站点从合适成人模型上的有效手动CPR开始。以明确角色、解剖核查及实际停顿测量准备并安装器械，而不只测总装配时间。

00:22:42.096 --> 00:22:54.456
Next introduce an unsafe fit. A good performance is recognizing the limit and promptly maintaining manual CPR, not forcing a successful-looking installation for the assessor.
接着加入不安全适配。好的表现是识别限制并迅速维持手动CPR，而不是为了考官眼中的成功安装而硬装。

00:22:54.456 --> 00:23:06.720
Then rehearse a planned battery replacement and state what indicator must return before restart. Finally introduce a stopped-device alarm and time how quickly effective manual support returns.
再练计划换电，说清重启前应回到哪一指示。最后加入器械停止报警，测量有效手动支持多快恢复。

00:23:06.720 --> 00:23:19.776
Review position, ventilation, analysis, safety and communication alongside timing. Improve one specific weakness and repeat; a short but unsafe run is not a pass.
复盘时把位置、通气、分析、安全、沟通与时间一起看。改一个具体弱点后重练，快速却不安全并不算通过。

00:23:19.776 --> 00:24:17.040
The recovered April 2026 compilation has a second, literal page track. Page 13 ends PR05 decontamination; 85 ends PR31 and 86 is PR32 vascular compression band; 581-584 continue N02, 585-587 contain N03, 588 opens N04 traumatic arrest, and 614-615 continue R02 with its diagram. These thirteen pages were read separately from the five named assignments. PR06 is still taught as a named procedure even though that numbered span does not contain its full standalone page. An index collision is not evidence that decontamination or a radial band is part of the N02 drug algorithm.
找回的2026年4月汇编还有第二条字面页码范围：13页是PR05去污结尾，85页是PR31结尾，86页为PR32血管压迫带；581至584续N02，585至587为N03，588开始N04创伤骤停，614至615续R02及流程图。这十三页与点名的五项分开阅读。PR06仍按点名操作教授，虽然上述页码范围不含其独立全文。索引碰撞不表示去污或桡动脉压迫带是N02药物流程的一部分。

00:24:17.040 --> 00:25:06.360
The decontamination ending explains a chain: move away from the hazard, safely remove contaminated clothing, reduce contamination and actively dry after wet methods. Emergency removal is immediate; gross decontamination uses larger water systems, and technical decontamination needs specialist resources. The source describes dry absorption as the default and selected wet methods with water no hotter than forty Celsius. That is not a command to apply water to every unknown chemical. Use incident-specific advice, protected specialists and safe access; communicate clearly and preserve warmth, dignity and assistance for people who cannot self-decontaminate. Do not bring secondary contamination into the ambulance.
去污结尾说明一条链：远离危险、安全移除污染衣物、减少污染，湿式处理后主动擦干。紧急去污重即时移除，粗去污使用较大型水系统，技术去污需要专门资源。来源以干式吸附为默认，并描述选定湿式方法及水温不超过40摄氏度；这不是对所有未知化学品都浇水的命令。应依事件特定建议、受保护专业人员及安全接近，清楚沟通，维护保暖、尊严，并协助不能自行去污者，避免把二次污染带进救护车。

00:25:06.360 --> 00:25:50.616
A vascular compression band controls a radial access site after trans-radial angiography; it is not a limb tourniquet for major traumatic bleeding. Learn two competing concerns: puncture-site hemostasis and adequate hand perfusion. Establish baseline observations and inspect pain, tingling, numbness, temperature, colour, refill, thumb oximetry and bleeding or hematoma. The recovered procedure specifies fifteen-minute checks. A thumb saturation number alone cannot exclude a vascular problem. During transfer, preserve the ordered wrist restrictions, comfort, access and monitoring and communicate new abnormalities promptly.
血管压迫带控制经桡动脉造影后的穿刺点，不是处理重大创伤出血的肢体止血带。要同时考虑两个问题：穿刺点止血与手部充分灌注。建立基线，检查疼痛、麻刺麻木、温度、颜色、再充盈、拇指血氧，以及出血或血肿。找回操作规定每15分钟检查，单个拇指饱和度不能排除血管问题。转运时维持规定腕部活动限制、舒适、通路及监测，及时通报新异常。

00:25:50.616 --> 00:26:33.096
For the specific band procedure, verify application time, the release-start instruction and the documented starting air volume before attempting release. The source describes a usual fifteen millilitres, an eighteen-millilitre maximum and removal of two millilitres every fifteen minutes with site reassessment. These are device/procedure-specific figures, not an instruction to inflate any wrist band to fifteen. If bleeding occurs during deflation, stop and restore the amount just removed under the applicable plan. Use the matching syringe and current instructions; an unclear product or handover requires clarification, not guessed deflation.
对这个特定压迫带操作，开始释放前要核实应用时间、开始放气指示及记录的起始空气量。来源描述通常15 mL、最多18 mL，每15分钟放2 mL并复查部位。这些是器械操作特定数字，不是让任何腕带都先充15 mL。放气中出血时，停止并按适用计划补回刚移除量。使用匹配注射器及现行说明；产品或交接不清时应澄清，不能猜着放气。

00:26:33.096 --> 00:27:27.456
The August 2026 PR32 card adds explicit complication pathways. For bleeding it limits inflation to eighteen millilitres; uncontrolled bleeding at that limit leads to band removal and proximal direct pressure, with hospital diversion if bleeding persists beyond ten minutes. It says not to reapply the band. With a hematoma and band still on, mark its extent, leave the band in place, apply directed pressure for ten minutes or longer and notify. Neurovascular compromise has a distinct one-millilitre release approach while hemostasis is preserved; lack of improvement prompts the nearest hospital. The card also allows a deflated band to remain during transfer for possible re-inflation. Document and notify the receiving team; do not improvise one adjustment for every complication.
2026年8月PR32卡加入明确并发症路径：出血时充气最多18 mL，到上限仍不能控制则移除压迫带并在近端直接压迫，超过10分钟仍出血则改送最近医院，且不重新应用该带。有血肿且带仍在时，应标记范围、保留带、按指示压迫10分钟或更久并通报。神经血管受损另有在保持止血条件下每次释放1 mL的路径，无改善则去最近医院。卡片还允许放气后的带留在转运途中，以备再次充气。应记录并通知接收团队，不能发明一套调整包办所有并发症。

00:27:27.456 --> 00:28:10.920
The N04 opening shifts the clinical mechanism: hemorrhage, hypoxemia and obstructed circulation can drive traumatic arrest, and a medical collapse can also precede the injury. Address the immediately relevant reversible cause and airway or bleeding problem in parallel, rather than allowing a mechanical-compression project to displace them. The source calls for consultation about treatment and conveyance and refers to trauma destination criteria. An organized rhythm without a pulse does not prove adequate flow, and a poor-prognosis association is not a complete discontinuation rule. PR31 excludes mechanical CPR in traumatic arrest.
N04开头改变临床机制：出血、低氧及循环阻塞可导致创伤骤停，也可能先有内科倒地再受伤。应并行处理当下相关可逆病因、气道或出血问题，不能让机械按压安装项目挤走这些处理。来源要求咨询治疗及转运，并参考创伤目的地标准。规则心律无脉搏不证明流量充分，差预后关联也不是完整终止规则。PR31排除创伤骤停的机械CPR。

00:28:10.920 --> 00:28:57.792
Read N04 general-body procedures with the provider-specific sections. The current PCP section says consider vascular access and a twenty-millilitre-per-kilogram bolus for hypovolemia; chest needle decompression appears under ACP, not as independent PCP authority. The opening also describes a selected penetrating-chest-trauma, PEA and short-to-trauma-centre situation where airway procedures must not delay conveyance, with fifteen-minute and Vancouver Coastal-Urban twenty-minute wording. These qualifications are not a universal clock for every injury. Escalate early, use the actual trauma pathway and reassess volume response rather than giving every arrest the same fluid or invasive treatment.
N04一般正文的操作必须结合等级段阅读。现行PCP段对低血容量写考虑通路及20 mL/kg液体推注，而胸部针减压列在ACP下，并非PCP独立权限。开头还描述特定穿透性胸伤、PEA及距创伤中心较短的情境，气道操作不应延误转运，并分别有15分钟及温哥华沿岸城区20分钟措辞。这些限定不是对每种创伤都通用的时钟。应尽早升级、使用真实创伤路径并复评补液反应，不能给所有骤停同样液体或侵入性操作。

00:28:57.792 --> 00:29:40.416
PR06 describes adult breaths of no more than five hundred to six hundred millilitres during CPR and a five-centimetre compression reference. They sit alongside rate, recoil, minimal pauses and the airway-dependent ventilation pattern. The practical objective is effective chest rise without overventilation, not emptying the whole bag to hit a memorized volume. Current adult depth teaching elsewhere uses five to six centimetres with avoidance of excess depth. PR06 palpation during ongoing compressions assesses generated flow; only the appropriately timed assessment of spontaneous circulation can establish ROSC.
PR06描述成人CPR每口气不超过500至600 mL，并用5厘米作为按压深度参考，同时要求频率、回弹、少停顿及随气道改变的通气模式。实操目标是有效胸廓起伏且不过度通气，不是为凑记忆容量挤完整个气囊。其他现行成人深度教学为5至6厘米并避免过深。PR06持续按压时触到的是产生的血流，只有在适当时点评估自主循环才可确立ROSC。

00:29:40.416 --> 00:30:26.976
Complete the N03 transition beyond the displayed oxygen targets. Reassess airway protection, glucose, pressure, temperature and the precipitating cause; its twenty-millilitre-per-kilogram fluid framework is a limit/context, not a routine volume for every patient. It describes thirty-degree head elevation where feasible, passive rather than large-volume cold-fluid cooling for suitable nontraumatic patients, and no passive cooling after traumatic arrest. Its destination guidance distinguishes suspected cardiac cause or STEMI and feasible PCI access from suspected noncardiac cause. Ongoing instability, the actual destination pathway and consultation still matter.
N03转换不只看显示的氧合目标，还要复评气道保护、血糖、压力、温度及原发病因；其20 mL/kg液体框架是限制和背景，不是每人常规量。它描述可行时抬头30度、适当非创伤患者被动而非大量冷液降温，以及创伤骤停后不被动降温。目的地指导区分疑似心源或STEMI且可合理到达PCI中心，与疑似非心源病因。持续不稳定、真实目的地路径及咨询仍重要。

00:30:26.976 --> 00:31:09.984
Original integration: compare three new situations without treating them as one algorithm: a contaminated collapsed patient, a post-angiography patient with a painful cool hand, and a bleeding trauma patient with PEA. State the immediate threat, safe assessment, relevant source and authority, then the observation or handover that would change the plan. Evidence tables in the compilation group linked research as supportive, neutral or against; those headings do not turn every listed intervention into a bedside order, and reading them is not an appraisal of every linked study. Keep the resuscitation, device and source timeline truthful.
原创整合：比较三种新情境，但不混成一个流程：污染后倒地患者、造影后疼痛冰冷手部患者，以及出血创伤伴PEA患者。说出即时威胁、安全评估、相关来源与权限，再说什么观察或交接会改变计划。汇编证据表把研究链接分为支持、中性或反对；这些标题不会把每个列项变成床边指令，读过标题也不等于评析每篇研究。复苏、器械与来源时序都要真实。

00:31:09.984 --> 00:31:23.232
Before leaving this lesson, explain the patient indication, service boundary and actual device fit. State why a motor operating regularly is not proof of adequate circulation or better survival.
结束前，应解释患者指征、机构边界及实际尺寸适配，并说明为何电机规律运动不证明灌注足够或存活更好。

00:31:23.232 --> 00:31:33.912
Talk through back plate, frame, cup location, height setting and mode while saying when effective compressions continue and when a pause is genuinely necessary.
应讲清背板、框架、吸盘位置、高度设置及模式，并同时说清何时有效按压继续、何时确有必要暂停。

00:31:33.912 --> 00:31:49.824
Correct the three important source shortcuts: the battery returns to PAUSE, not ADJUST; an interrupted twenty-second target is not adopted over the stricter school target; and retained post-ROSC standby is not a universal gold standard.
应纠正三个重要来源捷径：换电后回到PAUSE而非ADJUST；不能以二十秒代替较严格学校停顿目标；ROSC后保留待机并非统一金标准。

00:31:49.824 --> 00:32:02.712
Complete the actual instructor-led practical and exact device instructions before operational use. Competence includes the decision not to use the machine and the ability to restore manual care immediately.
操作使用前，还需完成真实教师带领实操及具体器械说明学习。能力也包括决定不用机器，以及立即恢复手动照护。
